图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness归档会话管理插件","id":"gh:1337384349","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-archive","slug":"imrascal/dsh-archive","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness归档会话管理插件"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# @imrascal/dsh-archive"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin that manages **archived sessions and the trash** from the settings p"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"pSeek Harness (DSH) plugin that manages **archived sessions and the trash** from the settings panel."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"- **Archived Sessions**: review sessions that are hidden from the sidebar but keep their records;\nre"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"store them individually or all at once, or move them to the trash.\n- **Trash**: review deleted sessi"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ons; restore, permanently purge, or empty the whole trash."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Deletes are **reversible**: deleting a session moves it to the trash (`~/.dsh/trash`); only\n*purge* "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"/ *empty trash* are permanent. Live (running) sessions refuse deletion with a clear message."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Or from a local checkout:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"**Restart the app** after installing (the host half loads at boot), then refresh the page —\nthe sect"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ion appears under Settings → Archived Sessions."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"> `dsh plugin` forwards to pnpm, so `pnpm` must be on your PATH."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"This feature originally lived as in-box patches across 12 files\n(`dsh-workspace`, `dsh-session-persi"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"stence-jsonl`, `dsh-host-apiproxy`, `dsh-client-runtime`,\n`dsh-client-ui-workspace`, ... — reference"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" diffs in `patches/`). This plugin re-implements\nit as a standalone package with a **dual-path desig"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"fs in `patches/`). This plugin re-implements\nit as a standalone package with a **dual-path design**:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Path | When | Behavior |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| **Native** | host/client already carry the archive API | the client calls `ctx.workspaces.unarchiv"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"eSession / trashList / ...` directly — same RPC + store-frame sync as the in-box implementation |\n| "},{"id":"p15s3","text":"**Fallback** | an app update reverted host or client to stock | the host half **patches at runtime**"},{"id":"p15s4","text":": adds the trash layer to `sessionPersistence` and the archive API to `workspaceRegistry`; the clien"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"t talks to the plugin's own `/dsh-archive/session` HTTP route |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"So the feature **survives app updates**: trash data lives in `~/.dsh/trash` (data, not code) and the"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"\narchive set lives in the workspace registry's persisted state. Whatever the update does to the\npack"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ages, the plugin feature-detects at startup and fills in whatever is missing."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Layout"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Migrating from an in-box patch (optional)"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"If your DSH install already carries the local archive-management patches (as this repo's dev\nmachine"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" did), the plugin and the in-box patch would register the same `archived-sessions` section.\nTo migra"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"d), the plugin and the in-box patch would register the same `archived-sessions` section.\nTo migrate:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"1. Restore `node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace/lib/client.js` to the official\nrelease"},{"id":"p21s2","text":" (drops the embedded ArchivedSessionsSection registration; the host patches may stay —\nthe plugin de"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"tects them and no-ops).\n2. Install and restart this plugin.\n3. The plugin stands down automatically "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"when the same section id already exists; once the in-box\npatch is removed the plugin takes over."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"> To move the host side back to stock as well, back up `~/.dsh` first, reverse `patches/`, and let\n>"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" this plugin's host half re-add the backend. Trash data and the archive set are unaffected."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Data safety"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- Deleting a session moves it to `~/.dsh/trash/<sessionId>-<timestamp>/`, restorable at any time.\n- "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"*Delete permanently* / *Empty trash* are irreversible — both are guarded by a confirmation modal.\n- "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"Attachments are content-addressed and shared; deleting a session never deletes attachments.\n- Live s"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"essions cannot be deleted (`session-live`); the UI explains what to do."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- Target DSH: `0.1.0-rc.5` and later — both the **native Web UI** (`dsh web` in a browser) and the\n*"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"*desktop GUI** (Electron window), which share the same host services and client bundle.\n- Stock host"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"s (rc.5 unpatched, rc.6): the host half adds the trash layer and the registry API at\nruntime; the cl"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"ient falls back to `/dsh-archive/session`.\n- Hosts that already carry the feature — rc.5 with the in"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"-box patches, and hosts where upstream\nmerged the same backend (persistence trash layer, registry `u"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"narchiveSession/deleteSession/\ntrash*`, API-proxy routes, client-runtime methods): every step featur"},{"id":"p26s7","text":"e-detects and no-ops; the\nclient calls the native `ctx.workspaces` API directly. Service availabilit"},{"id":"p26s8","text":"y is checked per call,\nso a service that is provided late is picked up automatically instead of stra"},{"id":"p26s9","text":"nding the section on\nthe fallback path.\n- **Partial native archive API (0.2.4)**: upstream ships the"},{"id":"p26s10","text":" registry API piecemeal — DSH\n`0.1.7-rc.1` has `archiveSession`/`unarchiveSession` natively but no `"},{"id":"p26s11","text":"deleteSession` and no trash\nlayer at all. The plugin now feature-detects every method on its own: it"},{"id":"p26s12","text":" fills exactly the gaps\n(here: `deleteSession` + `trashList/trashRestore/trashPurge/trashEmpty` plus"},{"id":"p26s13","text":" the persistence trash\nlayer) and never replaces a native method. 0.2.3 and earlier treated a native"},{"id":"p26s14","text":" `unarchiveSession`\nas proof that the whole API existed, skipped the patch, and every delete failed "},{"id":"p26s15","text":"with\n`workspace registry backend is not available yet`.\n- `deleteSession` is **fail-closed**: it ref"},{"id":"p26s16","text":"uses to run unless the persistence layer is trash-aware,\nso the plugin can never drive a stock hard-"},{"id":"p26s17","text":"delete backend (nothing is removed on refusal).\n- Host half shape-guards every patch; unrecognized s"},{"id":"p26s18","text":"ervices are skipped with a log line, never fatal.\n- **Cordis 4 strict inject (0.2.1)**: DSH Desktop "},{"id":"p26s19","text":"ships `@deepseek-ai/cordis` 4.x, where reading a\nservice property off a context (`ctx.sessionPersist"},{"id":"p26s20","text":"ence`) is only allowed when the current fiber\ndeclares it in `inject`; undeclared reads throw `canno"},{"id":"p26s21","text":"t get property \"X\" without inject`. The host\nhalf resolves services through `ctx.get(...)` and throu"},{"id":"p26s22","text":"gh the patched methods' receiver\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
